# Variables read by apps/mobile.
#
# The repository root .env is the single file used in local development; this
# lists what this application requires from it. Values here are local defaults
# only. Deployed builds supply their own at build time.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ means public. Everything under that prefix is substituted into
# the JavaScript bundle when the app is built, and a value shipped in a binary
# is discoverable (security.md:1655). Addresses belong here. A credential never
# does.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the backends are
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two addresses because there are two backends: REST to the authoritative API,
# GraphQL to the read-only Timeline aggregator.
#
# Which host works depends on where the app is running, and this is the single
# most common reason a development build cannot reach a machine that is plainly
# serving requests:
#
#   iOS simulator     localhost          — shares the host's network
#   Android emulator  10.0.2.2           — the emulator's alias for the host
#   Physical device   the host's LAN IP  — e.g. 192.168.1.24; the phone is not
#                                          on the host, and localhost is itself
#
# Both must be reachable from the same place: the app talks to both.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEED_URL=http://localhost:4000
